      "body": "\r\n\r\n\r\n## Purpose\r\n\r\nDeepSeek V4 owns its attention call and registers directly into static_forward_context, so it never reaches @maybe_transfer_kv_layer and never gets the connector wait that decorator provides. With a layer-wise KV connector the asynchronous loads are then unordered against the compute that reads them, and the model reads KV that has not landed.\r\n\r\nAdd maybe_wait_for_kv_layer() alongside maybe_transfer_kv_layer, carrying the same guards, and call it from DeepseekV4Attention._prepare_and_attn before the KV insert, the indexer and the compressor touch this layer's caches.\r\n\r\n## Test Plan\r\n\r\n## Test Result\r\n\r\n---\r\n<details>\r\n<summary> Essential Elements of an Effective PR Description Checklist </summary>\r\n\r\n- [ ] The purpose of the PR, such as \"Fix some issue (link existing issues this PR will resolve)\".\r\n- [ ] The test plan, such as providing test command.\r\n- [ ] The test results, such as pasting the results comparison before and after, or e2e results\r\n- [ ] (Optional) The necessary documentation update, such as updating `supported_models.md` and `examples` for a new model.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n",
